  <h2>Deep Notes</h2>
  <p>LSO VM Notes</p>
  <p>This function does not count free memory, and the name of this function makes this function difficult for people to learn. People say this function may be redefined or superseded by another more useful function when the LSL VM moves to <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/Mono" target="_blank">Mono</a>.</p>
  <p>We can concisely specify llGetFreeMemory in the context of the classic Unix model for a parallel task/ thread/ process. Think of the task of the script always holding 16384 bytes (16 KiB). Let the byte code and then stack grow up from the bottom, let the heap grow down from the top. llGetFreeMemory then returns the &quot;historic lowest heap pointer minus the stack end pointer&quot;.</p>
  <p>llGetFreeMemory does not count the bytes freed, llGetFreeMemory instead counts all the bytes never yet used.</p>
